$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 05/Design recognition

::EPI-W5-001::A survey measures current smoking and current hypertension during one visit. What design is this? {
=Cross-sectional study#Correct. Exposure and outcome are measured at essentially the same time.
~Cohort study#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
~Case-control study#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
~Randomised trial#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
}

::EPI-W5-002::Which feature most strongly identifies a cross-sectional study? {
=Exposure and outcome are assessed at the same time point or short period#Correct.
~Participants are selected by outcome status#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
~Participants are randomised#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
~Everyone is followed until disease occurs#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
}

$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 05/Prevalence

::EPI-W5-003::A cross-sectional survey finds 50 current cases among 500 participants. What is the prevalence? {
=10.0%#Correct. Prevalence is current cases divided by the population observed.
~11.1%#Use existing cases in the numerator and the contemporaneous population in the denominator.
~12.0%#Use existing cases in the numerator and the contemporaneous population in the denominator.
~100.0%#Use existing cases in the numerator and the contemporaneous population in the denominator.
}

