$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 05/Population and sampling

::EPI-W5-017::What is the target population? {
=The population about which the study intends to make an inference#Correct.
~Only those who returned completed questionnaires#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
~The list used to draw the sample#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
~The variable recorded on each respondent#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
}

::EPI-W5-018::What is a sampling frame? {
=The operational list or mechanism from which units are selected#Correct.
~The final regression model#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
~The target effect measure#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
~The response rate#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
}

::EPI-W5-019::A district household survey samples villages first and households within villages. Which feature must be considered in variance estimation for scenario 1? {
=Clustering of observations within selected villages#Correct. Clustered observations are not generally independent.
~Only the final sample size#Multistage cluster sampling affects standard errors.
~The alphabetical order of villages#Multistage cluster sampling affects standard errors.
~Whether prevalence exceeds 50%#Multistage cluster sampling affects standard errors.
}

