$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 05/Survey analysis

::EPI-W5-027::Prevalence is 15% in Group A and 10% in Group B. Which pair is closest to the prevalence ratio and prevalence difference? {
=PR 1.50; PD 5 percentage points#Correct. PR divides prevalences; PD subtracts them.
~PR 5.00; PD 1.50 percentage points#Ratio uses division; absolute difference uses subtraction.
~PR 0.67; PD 5 percentage points#Ratio uses division; absolute difference uses subtraction.
~PR 1.50; PD 25 percentage points#Ratio uses division; absolute difference uses subtraction.
}

