$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 05/Interpretation

::EPI-W5-044::A cross-sectional study finds higher current depression among heavy social-media users. Which conclusion is most defensible? {
=Heavy social-media use was associated with higher depression prevalence in the sample#Correct.
~Heavy social-media use caused depression#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
~Depression caused social-media use#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
~The association proves a treatment effect#Review the defining design or interpretation logic.
}

::EPI-W5-045::Which statement best reflects an appropriate use of a cross-sectional health-facility assessment? {
=Estimate the current proportion of facilities meeting a readiness standard#Correct. Cross-sectional assessment is well suited to current prevalence/readiness.
~Estimate five-year incidence without historical data#Match the design to a snapshot question.
~Prove a readiness intervention caused change#Match the design to a snapshot question.
~Measure survival time#Match the design to a snapshot question.
}

